  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\alpha+i \\beta$ and $\\gamma+i \\delta$ are the roots of $x^2-(3-2 i) x-(2 i-2)=0, i=\\sqrt{-1}$, then $\\alpha \\gamma+\\beta \\delta$ is equal to :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$-2$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$6$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$-6$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & x^2-(3-2 \\mathrm{i}) \\mathrm{x}-(2 \\mathrm{i}-2)=0 \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{(3-2 \\mathrm{i}) \\pm \\sqrt{(3-2 \\mathrm{i})^2-4(1)(-(2 \\mathrm{i}-2))}}{2(1)} \\\\ & ==\\frac{(3-2 \\mathrm{i}) \\pm \\sqrt{9-4-12 \\mathrm{i}+8 \\mathrm{i}-8}}{2} \\\\ & ==\\frac{3-2 \\mathrm{i} \\pm \\sqrt{-3-4 \\mathrm{i}}}{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{3-2 \\mathrm{i} \\pm \\sqrt{(1)^2+(2 \\mathrm{i})^2-2(1)(2 \\mathrm{i})}}{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{3-2 \\mathrm{i} \\pm(1-2 \\mathrm{i})}{2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\frac{3-2 \\mathrm{i}+1-2 \\mathrm{i}}{2} \\text { or } \\frac{3-2 \\mathrm{i}-1+2 \\mathrm{i}}{2} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 2-2 \\mathrm{i} \\text { or } 1+0 \\mathrm{i} \\\\ & \\text { So } \\alpha \\gamma+\\beta \\delta=2(1)+(-2)(0)=2\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}